WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:14.626
Over the next few days, Dan was moodier than usual.

2
00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:20.251
As for Tommy, he cut Nat out of his egg business.

3
00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:24.374
"I can't trust you anymore," Tommy said.

4
00:00:24.394 --> 00:00:27.456
"But I didn't take your money!"

5
00:00:27.877 --> 00:00:28.817
Nat protested.

6
00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:34.953
Tommy scrubbed "Tommy Bangs Company" from the barn wall.

7
00:00:34.973 --> 00:00:38.555
"And don't go stealing any of my eggs!"

8
00:00:38.575 --> 00:00:40.335
"I wouldn't!

9
00:00:40.615 --> 00:00:45.257
Tommy, wait Nat called after his friend as he ran from the barn.

10
00:00:48.118 --> 00:00:53.721
Several mornings later all the boys were playing in the barn while Tommy tried to gather eggs.

11
00:00:53.741 --> 00:00:59.963
"Those stupid hens have moved their nests, and I can't find any eggs!"

12
00:01:00.243 --> 00:01:01.544
he complained loudly.

13
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.263
"At least the hens trusted me," Nat said to himself.

14
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:09.966
"Tommy, come quick!"

15
00:01:10.406 --> 00:01:11.247
Demi shouted.

16
00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.829
"Look what I found!"

17
00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:19.414
Tommy ran to where Demi was pointing to a paper on the floor.

18
00:01:20.815 --> 00:01:25.479
Next to the words "For Tommy Bangs" were four quarters.

19
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.182
Tommy's eyes widened in surprise.

20
00:01:29.202 --> 00:01:31.864
"Where did those come from?"

21
00:01:35.232 --> 00:01:36.733
Demi glanced at Nat.

22
00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:39.754
"The thief must have put them there."

23
00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.456
Nat was tired of being a suspect.

24
00:01:44.476 --> 00:01:48.678
"How could I do that when I didn't take them in the first place?"

25
00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:53.640
Dan wandered over to see what was happening.

26
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.921
"It doesn't matter who took them.

27
00:01:56.481 --> 00:01:59.142
What's important is that everyone can be friends with Nat again."

28
00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:04.256
That night at supper, Mr.

29
00:02:04.296 --> 00:02:07.837
Bauer found a package on his chair with a note attached.

30
00:02:09.318 --> 00:02:13.179
While the professor read the note, Demi ripped open the package.

31
00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:17.800
"This is the book Uncle Laurie gave Dan!"

32
00:02:19.441 --> 00:02:25.242
Demi held up the book for all to see, while Dan turned red and stared at the table.

33
00:02:25.262 --> 00:02:28.964
"What does the note say, dear?"

34
00:02:29.324 --> 00:02:30.024
Jo asked.

35
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:32.741
"Our neighbor Mrs.

36
00:02:32.841 --> 00:02:38.526
Bates was concerned because her son purchased this book from Dan for a dollar," the professor said.

37
00:02:38.546 --> 00:02:42.870
"She's returning it because she thinks it's worth more than that.

38
00:02:47.153 --> 00:02:48.775
Did you sell your book, Dan?"

39
00:02:48.795 --> 00:02:52.878
"Yes, sir," Dan said slowly.

40
00:02:52.898 --> 00:02:56.041
"I owed somebody some money."

41
00:02:56.061 --> 00:02:59.464
"Who?" the professor asked.

42
00:03:01.032 --> 00:03:06.534
"Tommy." "Did you put those quarters in the barn this morning?"

43
00:03:08.115 --> 00:03:09.136
Dan looked Mr.

44
00:03:09.176 --> 00:03:10.136
Bauer in the eye.

45
00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.397
"Yes, I did."

46
00:03:13.557 --> 00:03:20.060
Tommy dropped his mug with a crash while Daisy said, "I knew Nat wasn't the thief!"

47
00:03:23.842 --> 00:03:28.584
Jo left the room looking so disappointed that Dan couldn't bear it.

48
00:03:29.888 --> 00:03:35.069
He hid his face in his hands for a moment and then looked up defiantly.

49
00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:42.071
"I'm the thief," Dan snapped, "and now that I've confessed, I'll return the money to Mrs.

50
00:03:42.151 --> 00:03:44.372
Bates, but I won't discuss this anymore!"

51
00:03:44.392 --> 00:03:48.073
"Not even to say that you're sorry?"

52
00:03:49.233 --> 00:03:54.755
Mr. Bauer was troubled by the change in Dan's attitude, which had been so positive lately.

53
00:03:56.095 --> 00:03:58.776
Dan shoved the table as he pushed back his chair.

54
00:04:00.108 --> 00:04:01.048
"I'm not sorry!"

55
00:04:01.308 --> 00:04:03.189
he cried, fleeing the room.

56
00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:08.951
"At least we know you didn't do it," the professor said to Nat.

57
00:04:08.971 --> 00:04:12.752
"I apologize for doubting that you told the truth."

58
00:04:14.412 --> 00:04:17.073
"I'm sorry too," Tommy said to Nat.

59
00:04:18.013 --> 00:04:20.574
"Do you want to be partners in the egg business again?"

60
00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:27.456
Nat nodded but said sorrowfully, "I wish the thief was anybody but Dan."

61
00:04:29.956 --> 00:04:36.401
Days passed, and Dan went about his work, silent, grim, and unrepentant.

62
00:04:36.421 --> 00:04:45.347
"The theft was bad enough," Jo said to her husband, "but to lie about it and then let

63
00:04:45.487 --> 00:04:47.068
Nat take the consequences.

64
00:04:47.088 --> 00:04:49.089
That was even worse!"

65
00:04:49.109 --> 00:04:53.132
"I agree," the professor said.

66
00:04:53.152 --> 00:04:58.336
"And Dan has stubbornly refused to talk about it or apologize."

67
00:04:59.944 --> 00:05:07.466
"I had such high hopes for Dan, but now Jo's voice trailed off, and she looked worried and

68
00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:14.668
sad. That afternoon Dan came upon the other boys playing in the birch grove.

69
00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:22.731
They were climbing a birch tree, grabbing slender, bendable branches, and swinging down to the ground.

70
00:05:24.631 --> 00:05:27.272
Dan stopped to watch as Jack took his turn.

71
00:05:29.448 --> 00:05:36.334
Unfortunately Jack had chosen to climb out on a high, thick branch—too thick to bend or swing.

72
00:05:38.616 --> 00:05:42.139
Now he was stuck there, dangling from a dangerous height.

73
00:05:42.159 --> 00:05:44.861
"You're going to fall!"

74
00:05:45.121 --> 00:05:46.723
Tommy cried from the ground.

75
00:05:46.743 --> 00:05:48.604
"Go back!"

76
00:05:50.066 --> 00:05:53.248
Jack tried to do that, but his hands kept slipping.

77
00:05:57.944 --> 00:06:01.587
"I can't hold on much longer!"

78
00:06:03.528 --> 00:06:05.549
Demi's face was white with fear.

79
00:06:05.569 --> 00:06:08.552
"You'll get killed if you fall!"

80
00:06:08.572 --> 00:06:11.373
"I'll help you!"

81
00:06:12.534 --> 00:06:16.697
Dan scrambled up the tree and was soon dangling from Jack's branch.

82
00:06:19.179 --> 00:06:23.522
Dan's weight bent the branch, and Jack dropped safely to the ground.

83
00:06:24.582 --> 00:06:28.989
But the branch flew up so suddenly that Dan lost his grip and fell.

84
00:06:30.929 --> 00:06:37.391
Pale and dizzy, he sat up slowly, while the boys gathered around him in admiration.

85
00:06:37.411 --> 00:06:39.752
"You saved my life!"

86
00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:40.752
Jack said.

87
00:06:40.772 --> 00:06:48.154
"It was nothing," Dan muttered, brushing himself off and walking slowly away.

88
00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.015
The next morning Mr.

89
00:06:52.055 --> 00:06:57.697
Bauer bounded into the schoolroom and practically shouted, "Dan is not the thief!"

90
00:06:59.918 --> 00:07:02.200
He shook Dan's hand and apologized.

91
00:07:03.821 --> 00:07:07.143
Tommy looked puzzled, asking, "Then who is?"

92
00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:10.965
The professor pointed to an empty seat.

93
00:07:10.985 --> 00:07:16.848
"Jack went home early this morning, but he left me a note confessing to the crime.

94
00:07:18.889 --> 00:07:23.012
He was peeking through a crack in the barn when he saw Tommy hide the money.

95
00:07:24.456 --> 00:07:28.398
After Dan saved his life, Jack couldn't stay silent any longer."

96
00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:33.221
Nat went over and stood by his old friend.

97
00:07:33.241 --> 00:07:36.983
"Dan, I don't understand why you said you took the money."

98
00:07:38.784 --> 00:07:42.807
"I knew you weren't the thief, and I didn't like the way everyone was blaming you."

99
00:07:44.468 --> 00:07:45.969
Dan turned to the professor.

100
00:07:45.989 --> 00:07:51.392
"I'm sorry I lied, sir, but I did it for my friend.

101
00:07:52.748 --> 00:07:53.849
Does Mrs.

102
00:07:53.969 --> 00:07:55.070
Bauer know the truth?"

103
00:07:55.090 --> 00:08:01.075
"Yes!" Jo said from the doorway, looking ready to dance for joy.

104
00:08:01.095 --> 00:08:05.359
"Three cheers for Dan!"
